  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Localization**\n\nI\'m focusing on the cleanliness of the codebase. The references are surprisingly localized to just a few key files: the new centralized config in `/src/config/steering.ts`, the new geometry and steering curve module in `/src/engine/AimBoundary.ts`, and the game types in `/src/types/game.ts`. It\'s a satisfying level of encapsulation.\n\n\n**Refining Implementations**\n\nI\'m now diving into the implementation details. I\'m updating `GameSettings` and `FlightTelemetry` with new boundary telemetry fields. I\'m also wiring `DEFAULT_SETTINGS` and `loadSavedSettings` to `STEERING_CONFIG` in `/src/config/ships.ts`. I\'m starting to build out a more robust `FlightController`, separating displacement accumulation, and implementing viewport-relative reticle clamping and scaling. Next, I\'ll tackle the camera and HUD.\n\n\n**Planning Browser Testing**\n\nI\'m now strategizing browser testing. I plan to check for Playwright or Chromium in the environment or devise a headless browser verification. In `DEV` mode, I\'ll leverage a read-only diagnostic getter on `window` or inspect DOM attributes and telemetry. I\'ll use existing test IDs like `aim-boundary-frame` and `virtual-mouse-cursor` to check steering. Finally, I will expose a `import.meta.env.DEV`-only `window.__STARFALL_TEST_HOOK__` in `App.tsx` for automated telemetry inspection.\n\n\n**Verifying Details**\n\nI\'m now focused on verifying the new modules. I\'ll need to test real `mousemove` events in Chromium, particularly with pointer lock. I\'ll ensure the test hook exposes state only in DEV mode. Also, I\'m carefully reviewing the `/src/config/steering.ts` module design: I\'m making sure `STEERING_CONFIG` has reasonable settings for `aimBoundaryWidth`, `aimBoundaryHeight`, `aimBoundaryCornerRadius`, `normalSensitivity`, `boundarySensitivity`, and `maxSensitivity`, and that the calculations are correct.\n\n\n**Defining Steering Behavior**\n\nI\'ve fleshed out `STEERING_CONFIG` with precise details. I\'m focusing on new factors, including `accelerationDistance`, `responseCurveExponent`, `recoverySmoothingSec`, `deadzone`, `precisionExponent`, `boundaryBlendStart`, and `softOutwardCompressionStart`. I also implemented `inwardExcessReturnFactor`, `maxSafeYawMultiplier` and `maxSafePitchMultiplier`. Finally, I\'ve specified bounds for `STEERING_BOUNDS` parameters.\n\n\n**Refining Aim Boundary**\n\nI\'m now carefully designing the `AimBoundary` module. The goal is zero per-frame allocations, with every helper function writing into a mutable `out` object. I am creating `RoundedRectBoundary` with calculations and clamping. I\'m focusing on viewport width/height, fraction clamping, and the corner radius calculation.\n\n\n**Calculating Boundary Dimensions**\n\nI\'m now calculating boundary dimensions based on viewport size. I\'m using formulas to derive `widthPx`, `heightPx`, and `cornerRadiusPx` using viewport width (`vw`) and height (`vh`) and rounding ratios. I\'m also determining `innerHalfW` and `innerHalfH` by considering the corner radius to find distances.\n\n\n**Evaluating Clamping Logic**\n\nI\'m now carefully examining the clamping logic within `clampToRoundedRect`. I\'m verifying the calculations step-by-step, paying close attention to the variables and their relationships. I\'m focused on the calculations for `axisBoundaryX`, `axisBoundaryY`, `normalizedX`, and `normalizedY` to ensure the reticle stays within the boundaries. I want to be certain the viewport dimensions are being considered properly.\n\n\n**Refining Corner Calculations**\n\nI\'m now refining the corner calculations, specifically the `clampToRoundedRect` function. I am meticulously reviewing the logic for orthogonal projections onto the circular corner arcs. The `sdf`, or signed distance field, is a key metric, and I am triple-checking the edge and corner clamping conditions. I\'m focusing on the calculations with the variables `qx`, `qy`, and `r`.\n\n\n**Validating Edge Cases**\n\nI\'m now focusing on a specific edge case in the `clampToRoundedRect` function. I\'m verifying the clamping calculations with `rawX = 350` and `rawY = 200`, well outside the top-right corner, while `halfW = 288, halfH = 162, r = 40.5, innerHalfW = 247.5, innerHalfH = 121.5`. I\'m tracing the variable values such as `qx = 102.5 > 0` and `qy = 78.5`. I\'m focused on the calculations for `dxCorner` and `axisBoundaryY`, to make sure everything clamps correctly.\n\n\n**Verifying Edge Clamping**\n\nI\'m now tracing the exact calculations through more edge case scenarios in `clampToRoundedRect`. I\'ve added more test data to ensure correct clamping for both inside and outside positions, as well as the behavior on edges. I\'ve focused on `qx`, `qy`, `sdf`, `clampedX`, and `clampedY`. I\'m especially focused on corner arc projections and edge cases that cause negative values, making sure those return valid results.\n\n\n\n**Confirming Corner Precision**\n\nI\'m now satisfied with the edge case calculations; the clamping is precise. The edge conditions and corner arcs are correctly calculated in `clampToRoundedRect`. Now, I\'m verifying `evaluateProgressiveAxisSensitivity`, which I\'ll test with a set of example values for all the parameters.\n\n\n**Testing Sensitivity Blending**\n\nI\'m now focusing on validating the sensitivity blending calculations. I\'m using an extensive suite of tests with carefully chosen parameter sets. I\'m especially focused on the transition between normal, boundary, and maximum sensitivity. I\'m making sure `evaluateProgressiveAxisSensitivity` smoothly transitions the `targetSensitivity` value, and the boundary conditions.\n\n\n\n**Validating Parameter Transitions**\n\nThe sensitivity blending tests have been exhaustive, revealing the elegance of the C1 continuity. I\'m satisfied. Now, I\'ll turn to implementing the updated files: `steering.ts`, `AimBoundary.ts`, and I\'ll revisit `game.ts`, `ships.ts`, `FlightController.ts`, and `CameraController.ts`.\n\n\n\n"
