    thinking: "**Refining Key Components**\n\nI\'m currently focused on refining crucial components: `/src/engine/FlightController.ts`, `/src/engine/CameraController.ts`, and `/src/scene/GameScene.tsx`. My efforts are concentrated on updating and refining the interactions and flow between these modules, ensuring smooth integration. I\'ve also identified key areas in the `/src/components/FlightHUD.tsx` and `/src/components/SettingsPanel` that need attention, and will be incorporating those shortly.\n\n\n**Adding Test Harness**\n\nI\'m now integrating a read-only test handle within `/src/App.tsx`. This addition is specifically for our automated headless tests, enabling them to assert precise live flight telemetry, pointer lock state, boundary math, and resize updates without impacting the production code. I\'m also reviewing `/src/engine/FlightController.ts` again, focusing on clean separation of concerns: input reception, boundary computation, and proportional scaling on viewport resize.\n\n\n**Implementing Mouse Smoothing**\n\nI\'m currently working on smoothing the mouse input within the `/src/engine/CameraController.ts` file, leveraging the previous clamp states, `excessX` and `excessY`. I\'m using the `accumulateAxisDisplacement` helper to manage this. I\'m focusing on ensuring smooth, non-explosive behavior during prolonged mouse movements and also addressing the issues caused by hard mouse input limits.\n\n\n**Refining Boundary Behavior**\n\nI\'m now refining the boundary behavior, particularly concerning the interaction between `inwardGain` and `excessPx`. The goal is to ensure a smooth transition and responsive behavior near the boundaries. I\'m focusing on precisely how `inwardGain` applies to `stepPx` when clearing `excessPx`, and how the remaining movement operates within the precision boundary. I\'m also carefully checking edge and corner behavior.\n\n\n**Analyzing Boundary Logic**\n\nI\'m now analyzing the logic for boundary calculations. I\'ve noticed an edge case, a movement purely down when the X axis is outside the right boundary. The current approach with `excessY` seems independent, allowing a 1:1 mapping. My focus now is on confirming the clamping to a rounded rectangle via `clampToRoundedRect()`, which provides `clampedX, clampedY` that will never be stretched beyond the rounded rectangle. I\'m also ensuring the telemetry reflects this behavior. Finally, I will evaluate the progressive steering independently per axis.\n\n\n**Implementing Flight Physics**\n\nI\'m now implementing flight physics, focusing on ship yaw and pitch rates. I\'m leveraging clamped normalized deflection and smoothed progressive sensitivity to preserve the Phase 1/2 flight physics. This incorporates yaw/pitch/roll angular damping, local-space quaternions, visual bank, boost energy, and thrust/drag/lateral grip. I\'m working to make sure everything works with the existing clamp states and smoothing. I also plan to check the corner markings in `FlightHUD.tsx`.\n\n\n\n**Designing Cockpit Arcs**\n\nI\'m now designing the cockpit\'s visual boundaries using a series of SVG path commands. I\'m focusing on crafting four subtle sci-fi corner arcs that trace the rounded rectangle\'s boundary, avoiding a prominent box. I\'ve defined the geometry with `halfW`, `halfH`, and corner radius `r`, and am using `arm` for straight arm extension. My work involves calculating the precise `M` and `L` coordinates for the SVG path strings of each corner.\n\n\n"
