  planner_response {
    response: "Implemented the final viewport-relative `45% \303\227 45%` rounded-rectangle aiming boundary and refined its integration with STARFALL\'s progressive mouse steering and preserved Pointer Lock pipeline.\n\n### 1. Files and Systems Changed\n- **Centralized Steering Config** (`src/config/steering.ts`): Added single source of truth (`STEERING_CONFIG`, `STEERING_BOUNDS`) for aim boundary dimensions (`45% \303\227 45%`), corner radius ratio, normal/boundary/max sensitivity, acceleration distance, curve exponent, and recovery smoothing.\n- **Rounded-Rectangle Boundary & Progressive Curve** (`src/engine/AimBoundary.ts`): Created pure zero-allocation module handling viewport-relative rounded-rectangle geometry (`computeRoundedRectBoundary`), C1-continuous closest-point clamping with preserved excess (`clampToRoundedRect`), and per-axis progressive sensitivity (`evaluateProgressiveAxisSensitivity`).\n- **Flight Simulation** (`src/engine/FlightController.ts`): Decoupled relative displacement accumulation, rounded-rectangle reticle clamping, progressive sensitivity smoothing, and ship yaw/pitch control; removed reticle overdrive stretch outside the boundary; added proportional displacement rescaling on viewport resize and soft outward compression / smooth inward excess unwinding with zero hard mouse input cutoff.\n- **Camera Follow** (`src/engine/CameraController.ts`): Preserved Phase 1 chase framing and boost FOV while scaling rotational tracking lambda gently with angular speed so rapid Zone C turns remain crisp without steering latency.\n- **Viewport Sync** (`src/scene/GameScene.tsx`): Passed live game viewport dimensions (`state.size.width`, `state.size.height`) into `FlightController.update`.\n- **HUD Indicator** (`src/components/FlightHUD.tsx`): Replaced the solid border box with subtle 4-corner rounded-rectangle SVG arc markings tracked to the game viewport via `ResizeObserver` (`pointer-events-none`, zero per-frame React re-renders).\n- **Types, Persistence & Settings UI** (`src/types/game.ts`, `src/config/ships.ts`, `src/components/SettingsPanel.tsx`, `src/App.tsx`): Updated `GameSettings` and `FlightTelemetry` fields, migrated saved settings to `v3` so the confirmed `45% \303\227 45%` defaults apply cleanly, wired the Settings curve preview and `45% \303\227 45%` Aim Boundary slider to the centralized config, and added a `DEV`-only read-only diagnostic handle for browser testing.\n- **Preserved Intact**: `src/engine/InputManager.ts` (Pointer Lock ownership, pure relative `movementX`/`movementY`, single-consumption frame snapshot, and >500px OS warp-spike filtering) was preserved untouched.\n\n### 2. Final Boundary Geometry and Dimensions\n- **Shape**: Centered rounded rectangle calculated from live game viewport dimensions $W \\times H$ (recalculated dynamically on resize).\n- **Width**: `45%` of viewport width \342\206\222 horizontal half-extent $0.225 \\times W$.\n- **Height**: `45%` of viewport height \342\206\222 vertical half-extent $0.225 \\times H$.\n- **Corner Radius**: Configurable ratio `0.25 \303\227 min(halfW, halfH)` (e.g., `40.5 px` at `1280\303\227720`, `43.2 px` at `1024\303\227768`, `33.75 px` at `1440\303\227600`).\n- **Visual Treatment**: Subtle 4-corner curved sci-fi SVG arc markings (faint cyan at rest, gentle opacity/tint cue near boundary and in transition/acceleration).\n\n### 3. Rounded-Rectangle Clamping\nGiven unconstrained relative virtual displacement $(x, y)$ from viewport center and inner arc-center box $(innerHalfW, innerHalfH) = (halfW - r, halfH - r)$:\n- Computes the exact Euclidean rounded-rectangle signed distance $d_{\\text{sdf}} = \\|(\\max(|x|-innerHalfW, 0), \\max(|y|-innerHalfH, 0))\\| + \\min(\\max(|x|-innerHalfW, |y|-innerHalfH), 0) - r$.\n- If $d_{\\text{sdf}} \\le 0$: the reticle tracks $(x, y)$ directly with zero excess.\n- If $d_{\\text{sdf}} > 0$:\n  - Straight horizontal/vertical edge regions clamp perpendicularly onto $\\pm halfW$ or $\\pm halfH$ without disturbing the parallel axis.\n  - Corner quadrants project orthogonally onto the circular corner arc of radius $r$ around $(\\pm innerHalfW, \\pm innerHalfH)$.\n- Because straight edges meet the corner arcs tangentially, reticle motion along the perimeter is C1-continuous with zero snapping, and the reticle never leaves the configured `45% \303\227 45%` rounded rectangle.\n\n### 4. Progressive Steering Beyond the Boundary\n- Clamping does not discard outward mouse movement: unconstrained `(virtualAimX, virtualAimY)` continues accumulating relative Pointer Lock deltas with no hard mouse input limit.\n- Independent per-axis outward excess `(excessX, excessY) = (|rawX - clampedX|, |rawY - clampedY|)` drives each axis independently:\n  - **Zone A (Precision)**: Core 85% of the boundary holds flat `1.0x` sensitivity; the outer 15% applies C1 smoothstep easing down to `boundarySensitivity` right at the curved perimeter (`axisBoundaryX`/`axisBoundaryY`).\n  - **Zone B (Transition)**: Immediately beyond the boundary, sensitivity starts at `0.35x` and rises smoothly via $f(e) = \\frac{e^p}{1 + e^p}$ where $e = \\text{excess} / S$.\n  - **Zone C (Accelerated Turning)**: Once $\\text{sensitivity}(e) \\ge 1.0$, continued outward movement progressively accelerates turn rate asymptotically toward `2.5x`.\n  - **Inward Return**: Pulling inward smoothly unwinds overdrive excess back to the boundary (without sticking after extended turns) and delta-time exponential recovery smoothing ($\\tau = 0.12\\text{ s}$) restores precision steering cleanly.\n\n### 5. Final Sensitivity and Acceleration Parameters\n| Parameter | Value |\n| --- | --- |\n| Aim Boundary Width / Height | `45%` \303\227 `45%` (`0.225W`, `0.225H` half-extents) |\n| Boundary Corner Radius Ratio | `0.25 \303\227 min(halfW, halfH)` |\n| Normal Sensitivity (Zone A) | `1.0` |\n| Boundary Sensitivity (Zone B entry) | `0.35` |\n| Maximum Sensitivity (Zone C asymptote) | `2.5` |\n| Acceleration Distance ($S$) | `240 px` |\n| Response Curve Exponent ($p$) | `2.0` |\n| Recovery Smoothing ($\\tau$) | `0.12 s` |\n\n### 6. Flight Handling Preservation\n- Preserved the responsive Phase 1 flight physics intact: local-space quaternion yaw/pitch/roll (zero gimbal lock), frame-rate-independent angular damping (`angularDamping * 2.1` steering / `1.8` release), A/D roll authority, visual yaw banking, lateral grip, passive drag, and boost energy/acceleration behavior.\n- Enhanced chase camera rotational tracking slightly at high angular speeds so Zone C accelerated turns maintain clear framing without extra latency.\n\n### 7. Actual Browser Testing Results\nVerified in headless Chromium against the running dev server (`npm run build` + `tsc --noEmit` also passed cleanly; **18/18 checks passed**, zero console or page errors):\n- **Pointer Lock**: Engaged natively on `<canvas>` (`document.pointerLockElement === canvas`), continued receiving relative deltas at physical screen edges (`clientX = 0 / 1279`, `clientY = 719`), and preserved >500px OS warp-spike filtering.\n- **1280\303\227720 (16:9)**: Verified exact `576 \303\227 324 px` (`45% \303\227 45%`), `r = 40.5 px`, 4 curved SVG arc markings matching engine geometry.\n- **Zone A \342\206\222 Zone B \342\206\222 Zone C**:\n  - Inside boundary (`rawX = 140 px`): `zone = precision`, `sensX = 1.000`, `excessX = 0`, active yaw.\n  - Boundary crossing (`rawX = 310 px`, `excessX = 22 px`): `zone = transition`, `sensX = 0.370`, reticle strictly at `screenX = 0.725`, independent `sensY = 1.000`, ship continued turning `+20.0\302\260` while held at boundary.\n  - Outward acceleration (`excessX = 262 px` \342\206\222 `742 px`): `zone = acceleration`, `sensX` climbed `1.518` \342\206\222 `2.296`, `|yawVelocity|` climbed `3.18` \342\206\222 `4.82 rad/s`, reticle stayed locked at `0.725`.\n- **Corner Clamping**: Diagonal push `(+700, +700)` clamped reticle to `(272.45, 153.40)` at exact distance `40.50 px` from corner arc center while preserving `excessX = 427.55 px`, `excessY = 546.60 px`.\n- **Inward Recovery**: Pulling inward from Zone C returned cleanly to `zone = precision`, `sensX = 1.000`, `excessX = 0`.\n- **Boost & Thrust**: Verified `W + Shift` engaged boost (`182.5 m/s`, energy drain, `boostIntensity = 0.999`).\n- **Multi-Aspect Resize**: Verified dynamic recalculation and clamping at `1024\303\227768` (4:3 \342\206\222 `460.8 \303\227 345.6 px`, `r = 43.2 px`) and `1440\303\227600` (21:9 \342\206\222 `648 \303\227 270 px`, `r = 33.75 px`).\n- **Settings UI**: Verified default `45% \303\227 45%`, `0.35x`, `2.50x`, `240 px`, and `p=2.0` readouts.\n\n### 8. Remaining Issues\n- None identified from automated Chromium testing or compilation/lint checks. Headless Chromium verified native Pointer Lock acquisition and synthetic edge-pinned relative mouse deltas, though physical mouse feel across varied desktop DPI/polling-rate hardware should still be sanity-checked manually during live playtesting to fine-tune `accelerationDistance` (`240 px`) or `boundarySensitivity` (`0.35`) if desired."
    thinking: "**Analyzing Test Results**\n\nI\'m incredibly pleased to report that all 18 tests have passed successfully within real headless Chromium! The specific output, especially regarding the Settings UI and Native Pointer Lock, is exemplary. The percentages, multipliers, pixel values, and the \'p\' parameter are all displaying as expected, representing textbook precision.\n\n\n**Examining the Boundary Logic**\n\nI\'ve been meticulously examining the behavior at the boundary, particularly with a 1280x720 aspect ratio. The calculations for boundary width and height in both the engine and HUD SVG are spot-on. The corner radius of the rounded rectangle is also as expected. I\'m seeing smooth transitions between zones, with sensitivity adjustments and clamping operating perfectly during transitions, and continuous turning demonstrating the correct calculations and responsiveness.\n\n\n**Refining Zone Transitions**\n\nI\'m now satisfied with the \'acceleration\' zone\'s performance at 2px, and 742px excess X values. The warp-spike filter remains active, effectively handling OS glitches. I\'ve also verified the rounded-rectangle corner clamping at (+700, +700), with precise distances. Moving inwards from Zone C, transition back to precision is now smooth. I\'ve also validated the boost and thrust functionality. Additionally, I\'ve confirmed resizing to 1024x768 (4:3) updates calculations.\n\n\n"
    message_id: "9iT_ao3kDJTBqtsPvPD5-A8"
    modified_response: "Implemented the final viewport-relative `45% \303\227 45%` rounded-rectangle aiming boundary and refined its integration with STARFALL\'s progressive mouse steering and preserved Pointer Lock pipeline.\n\n### 1. Files and Systems Changed\n- **Centralized Steering Config** (`src/config/steering.ts`): Added single source of truth (`STEERING_CONFIG`, `STEERING_BOUNDS`) for aim boundary dimensions (`45% \303\227 45%`), corner radius ratio, normal/boundary/max sensitivity, acceleration distance, curve exponent, and recovery smoothing.\n- **Rounded-Rectangle Boundary & Progressive Curve** (`src/engine/AimBoundary.ts`): Created pure zero-allocation module handling viewport-relative rounded-rectangle geometry (`computeRoundedRectBoundary`), C1-continuous closest-point clamping with preserved excess (`clampToRoundedRect`), and per-axis progressive sensitivity (`evaluateProgressiveAxisSensitivity`).\n- **Flight Simulation** (`src/engine/FlightController.ts`): Decoupled relative displacement accumulation, rounded-rectangle reticle clamping, progressive sensitivity smoothing, and ship yaw/pitch control; removed reticle overdrive stretch outside the boundary; added proportional displacement rescaling on viewport resize and soft outward compression / smooth inward excess unwinding with zero hard mouse input cutoff.\n- **Camera Follow** (`src/engine/CameraController.ts`): Preserved Phase 1 chase framing and boost FOV while scaling rotational tracking lambda gently with angular speed so rapid Zone C turns remain crisp without steering latency.\n- **Viewport Sync** (`src/scene/GameScene.tsx`): Passed live game viewport dimensions (`state.size.width`, `state.size.height`) into `FlightController.update`.\n- **HUD Indicator** (`src/components/FlightHUD.tsx`): Replaced the solid border box with subtle 4-corner rounded-rectangle SVG arc markings tracked to the game viewport via `ResizeObserver` (`pointer-events-none`, zero per-frame React re-renders).\n- **Types, Persistence & Settings UI** (`src/types/game.ts`, `src/config/ships.ts`, `src/components/SettingsPanel.tsx`, `src/App.tsx`): Updated `GameSettings` and `FlightTelemetry` fields, migrated saved settings to `v3` so the confirmed `45% \303\227 45%` defaults apply cleanly, wired the Settings curve preview and `45% \303\227 45%` Aim Boundary slider to the centralized config, and added a `DEV`-only read-only diagnostic handle for browser testing.\n- **Preserved Intact**: `src/engine/InputManager.ts` (Pointer Lock ownership, pure relative `movementX`/`movementY`, single-consumption frame snapshot, and >500px OS warp-spike filtering) was preserved untouched.\n\n### 2. Final Boundary Geometry and Dimensions\n- **Shape**: Centered rounded rectangle calculated from live game viewport dimensions $W \\times H$ (recalculated dynamically on resize).\n- **Width**: `45%` of viewport width \342\206\222 horizontal half-extent $0.225 \\times W$.\n- **Height**: `45%` of viewport height \342\206\222 vertical half-extent $0.225 \\times H$.\n- **Corner Radius**: Configurable ratio `0.25 \303\227 min(halfW, halfH)` (e.g., `40.5 px` at `1280\303\227720`, `43.2 px` at `1024\303\227768`, `33.75 px` at `1440\303\227600`).\n- **Visual Treatment**: Subtle 4-corner curved sci-fi SVG arc markings (faint cyan at rest, gentle opacity/tint cue near boundary and in transition/acceleration).\n\n### 3. Rounded-Rectangle Clamping\nGiven unconstrained relative virtual displacement $(x, y)$ from viewport center and inner arc-center box $(innerHalfW, innerHalfH) = (halfW - r, halfH - r)$:\n- Computes the exact Euclidean rounded-rectangle signed distance $d_{\\text{sdf}} = \\|(\\max(|x|-innerHalfW, 0), \\max(|y|-innerHalfH, 0))\\| + \\min(\\max(|x|-innerHalfW, |y|-innerHalfH), 0) - r$.\n- If $d_{\\text{sdf}} \\le 0$: the reticle tracks $(x, y)$ directly with zero excess.\n- If $d_{\\text{sdf}} > 0$:\n  - Straight horizontal/vertical edge regions clamp perpendicularly onto $\\pm halfW$ or $\\pm halfH$ without disturbing the parallel axis.\n  - Corner quadrants project orthogonally onto the circular corner arc of radius $r$ around $(\\pm innerHalfW, \\pm innerHalfH)$.\n- Because straight edges meet the corner arcs tangentially, reticle motion along the perimeter is C1-continuous with zero snapping, and the reticle never leaves the configured `45% \303\227 45%` rounded rectangle.\n\n### 4. Progressive Steering Beyond the Boundary\n- Clamping does not discard outward mouse movement: unconstrained `(virtualAimX, virtualAimY)` continues accumulating relative Pointer Lock deltas with no hard mouse input limit.\n- Independent per-axis outward excess `(excessX, excessY) = (|rawX - clampedX|, |rawY - clampedY|)` drives each axis independently:\n  - **Zone A (Precision)**: Core 85% of the boundary holds flat `1.0x` sensitivity; the outer 15% applies C1 smoothstep easing down to `boundarySensitivity` right at the curved perimeter (`axisBoundaryX`/`axisBoundaryY`).\n  - **Zone B (Transition)**: Immediately beyond the boundary, sensitivity starts at `0.35x` and rises smoothly via $f(e) = \\frac{e^p}{1 + e^p}$ where $e = \\text{excess} / S$.\n  - **Zone C (Accelerated Turning)**: Once $\\text{sensitivity}(e) \\ge 1.0$, continued outward movement progressively accelerates turn rate asymptotically toward `2.5x`.\n  - **Inward Return**: Pulling inward smoothly unwinds overdrive excess back to the boundary (without sticking after extended turns) and delta-time exponential recovery smoothing ($\\tau = 0.12\\text{ s}$) restores precision steering cleanly.\n\n### 5. Final Sensitivity and Acceleration Parameters\n| Parameter | Value |\n| --- | --- |\n| Aim Boundary Width / Height | `45%` \303\227 `45%` (`0.225W`, `0.225H` half-extents) |\n| Boundary Corner Radius Ratio | `0.25 \303\227 min(halfW, halfH)` |\n| Normal Sensitivity (Zone A) | `1.0` |\n| Boundary Sensitivity (Zone B entry) | `0.35` |\n| Maximum Sensitivity (Zone C asymptote) | `2.5` |\n| Acceleration Distance ($S$) | `240 px` |\n| Response Curve Exponent ($p$) | `2.0` |\n| Recovery Smoothing ($\\tau$) | `0.12 s` |\n\n### 6. Flight Handling Preservation\n- Preserved the responsive Phase 1 flight physics intact: local-space quaternion yaw/pitch/roll (zero gimbal lock), frame-rate-independent angular damping (`angularDamping * 2.1` steering / `1.8` release), A/D roll authority, visual yaw banking, lateral grip, passive drag, and boost energy/acceleration behavior.\n- Enhanced chase camera rotational tracking slightly at high angular speeds so Zone C accelerated turns maintain clear framing without extra latency.\n\n### 7. Actual Browser Testing Results\nVerified in headless Chromium against the running dev server (`npm run build` + `tsc --noEmit` also passed cleanly; **18/18 checks passed**, zero console or page errors):\n- **Pointer Lock**: Engaged natively on `<canvas>` (`document.pointerLockElement === canvas`), continued receiving relative deltas at physical screen edges (`clientX = 0 / 1279`, `clientY = 719`), and preserved >500px OS warp-spike filtering.\n- **1280\303\227720 (16:9)**: Verified exact `576 \303\227 324 px` (`45% \303\227 45%`), `r = 40.5 px`, 4 curved SVG arc markings matching engine geometry.\n- **Zone A \342\206\222 Zone B \342\206\222 Zone C**:\n  - Inside boundary (`rawX = 140 px`): `zone = precision`, `sensX = 1.000`, `excessX = 0`, active yaw.\n  - Boundary crossing (`rawX = 310 px`, `excessX = 22 px`): `zone = transition`, `sensX = 0.370`, reticle strictly at `screenX = 0.725`, independent `sensY = 1.000`, ship continued turning `+20.0\302\260` while held at boundary.\n  - Outward acceleration (`excessX = 262 px` \342\206\222 `742 px`): `zone = acceleration`, `sensX` climbed `1.518` \342\206\222 `2.296`, `|yawVelocity|` climbed `3.18` \342\206\222 `4.82 rad/s`, reticle stayed locked at `0.725`.\n- **Corner Clamping**: Diagonal push `(+700, +700)` clamped reticle to `(272.45, 153.40)` at exact distance `40.50 px` from corner arc center while preserving `excessX = 427.55 px`, `excessY = 546.60 px`.\n- **Inward Recovery**: Pulling inward from Zone C returned cleanly to `zone = precision`, `sensX = 1.000`, `excessX = 0`.\n- **Boost & Thrust**: Verified `W + Shift` engaged boost (`182.5 m/s`, energy drain, `boostIntensity = 0.999`).\n- **Multi-Aspect Resize**: Verified dynamic recalculation and clamping at `1024\303\227768` (4:3 \342\206\222 `460.8 \303\227 345.6 px`, `r = 43.2 px`) and `1440\303\227600` (21:9 \342\206\222 `648 \303\227 270 px`, `r = 33.75 px`).\n- **Settings UI**: Verified default `45% \303\227 45%`, `0.35x`, `2.50x`, `240 px`, and `p=2.0` readouts.\n\n### 8. Remaining Issues\n- None identified from automated Chromium testing or compilation/lint checks. Headless Chromium verified native Pointer Lock acquisition and synthetic edge-pinned relative mouse deltas, though physical mouse feel across varied desktop DPI/polling-rate hardware should still be sanity-checked manually during live playtesting to fine-tune `accelerationDistance` (`240 px`) or `boundarySensitivity` (`0.35`) if desired."
