  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Boundary Values**\n\nI\'ve just spotted two key details in `src/config/steering.ts`. The values for `aimBoundaryWidth` (0.40) and `aimBoundaryHeight` (0.45) are crucial. They represent the boundaries of the aiming area, expressed as a percentage of the viewport dimensions. Now, I see these translate to half-extents of 0.20 * W and 0.225 * H, respectively.\n\n\n**Refining Ratio Logic**\n\nI\'m now diving into `src/components/SettingsPanel.tsx`, specifically lines 290-293. I\'ve realized the Aim Boundary slider\'s behavior requires some fine-tuning. The single slider should maintain the 40:45 aspect ratio proportionally, avoiding a convoluted UI. I\'m exploring a formula to cleanly scale both width and height when adjusting the slider, ensuring a predictable user experience. I want to keep height from snapping back.\n\n\n**Implementing Versioning & Docs**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on data persistence. I see a potential conflict: older versions in `localStorage` could retain outdated aim boundary values. To avoid this, I\'ll bump the storage key to `starfall.settings.v4`, with `LEGACY_SETTINGS_KEY_V3` as a fallback. This will force a migration and apply the correct 40% x 45% boundary defaults. Finally, I\'ll update the comments across several files, including `steering.ts` and `game.ts`, to reflect these current boundary values and ensure clarity in documentation.\n\n\n"
    message_id: "3SX_as74LKO439IP6KbR0Q0"
