  planner_response {
    response: "Re-running the Chromium verification suite after restarting the dev server.\nUpdated STARFALL\'s aiming boundary width from `45%` to **`40%`** of the game viewport width while keeping the height at **`45%`** of the game viewport height, preserving the centered rounded-rectangle geometry, Pointer Lock implementation, progressive mouse steering, and flight feel.\n\n### 1. Files and Systems Changed\n- `src/config/steering.ts`: Changed `STEERING_CONFIG.aimBoundaryWidth` from `0.45` to `0.4` (`40%` width, half-extent `0.20 * W`) while keeping `aimBoundaryHeight` at `0.45` (`45%` height, half-extent `0.225 * H`).\n- `src/config/ships.ts`: Bumped settings storage key to `starfall.settings.v4` so cached `v1`\342\200\223`v3` browser settings migrate cleanly to the confirmed `40% \303\227 45%` boundary defaults while preserving other user preferences.\n- `src/components/SettingsPanel.tsx`: Updated the single Aim Boundary slider handler so adjusting boundary size preserves the configured `40:45` width-to-height aspect ratio (`height = clamp(round(width * (0.45 / 0.40)))`).\n- `src/types/game.ts`, `src/engine/AimBoundary.ts`, `src/engine/FlightController.ts`, `src/components/FlightHUD.tsx`: Updated inline documentation comments to reflect `40% \303\227 45%` dimensions.\n- Unrelated systems (`InputManager.ts`, combat, weapons, bot AI, missions, progression, flight physics, and camera controller) were not modified.\n\n### 2. Final Boundary Geometry and Dimensions\n- **Shape**: Centered rounded rectangle calculated dynamically from the live game viewport dimensions $W \\times H$.\n- **Width**: `40%` of viewport width (horizontal half-extent `0.20 \303\227 W`).\n- **Height**: `45%` of viewport height (vertical half-extent `0.225 \303\227 H`).\n- **Corner Radius**: `0.25 \303\227 min(halfW, halfH)`.\n\n### 3. Rounded-Rectangle Clamping & Progressive Steering\n- Unconstrained relative Pointer Lock displacement `(virtualAimX, virtualAimY)` continues accumulating without a hard cutoff, while `clampToRoundedRect` projects points outside the rounded rectangle onto its straight edges or tangential corner arcs (`r = 0.25 \303\227 min(halfW, halfH)`).\n- Independent per-axis outward excess `(excessX, excessY)` feeds `evaluateProgressiveAxisSensitivity` using $f(e) = \\frac{e^p}{1 + e^p}$ and $\\text{sensitivity}(e) = 0.35 + (2.5 - 0.35)\\,f(e)$ with `0.12 s` recovery smoothing.\n\n### 4. Verification Results\n- **Build & Type Check**: `npm run build` (`vite build`) and `tsc --noEmit` both succeeded with zero errors.\n- **Browser Testing (Headless Chromium on `http://localhost:3000`, 16/16 checks passed, zero console/page errors)**:\n  - **Settings UI**: Displays `40% \303\227 45%` Aim Boundary alongside `0.35x`, `2.50x`, `240 px`, and `p=2.0`.\n  - **Pointer Lock**: Engaged natively on `<canvas>`.\n  - **1280\303\227720 (16:9)**: Verified exact `512 \303\227 324 px` (`40% \303\227 45%`, half-extents `256 \303\227 162 px`, `r = 40.5 px`) on both engine state and subtle 4-corner SVG HUD markings.\n  - **Zone A / B / C & Corner Clamping**:\n    - Zone A (`rawX = 140 px`): `zone = precision`, `sensX = 1.000`, `excessX = 0`, active yaw.\n    - Zone B (`rawX = 278 px`, `excessX = 22 px`): `zone = transition`, `sensX = 0.371`, reticle clamped strictly at `screenX = 0.700`, `sensY = 1.000`, ship continued turning `+14.4\302\260` while held at boundary.\n    - Zone C (`excessX = 262 px` \342\206\222 `742 px`): `zone = acceleration`, `sensX` climbed `1.449` \342\206\222 `2.297`, `|yawVelocity|` climbed `3.04` \342\206\222 `4.82 rad/s`, reticle stayed locked at `screenX = 0.700`.\n    - Diagonal corner push `(+700, +700)` clamped onto circular corner arc at `(240.45, 153.40)` (`distFromCornerCenter = 40.50 px`) with `excessX = 459.55 px` and `excessY = 546.60 px`.\n    - Inward return cleanly restored `zone = precision` (`sensX = 1.000`, `excessX = 0`).\n  - **Viewport Resizes**: Verified dynamic recalculation and clamping at `1024\303\227768` (`409.6 \303\227 345.6 px`, `r = 43.2 px`) and `1440\303\227600` (`576 \303\227 270 px`, `r = 33.75 px`).\n\n### 5. Remaining Issues\n- None identified from compilation, type-checking, or automated Chromium testing."
    message_id: "oyb_apCfMeLI-sAPq66tqQY"
